{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeRankTwoMarkov","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeRankTwoMarkov","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Algebra.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Module.LinearMap.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Rat","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum"],"declarations":49,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeRankTwoMarkov.Hecke2.exists_nonmultiplicative","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeRankTwoMarkov.Hecke2.exists_nonmultiplicative","kind":"theorem","line":248,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeRankTwoMarkov.lean#L248-L256","doc":"A concrete non-degenerate instance over `ℚ`: at `h = 1`, `z = 0` the\nmultiplicativity defect is `1 ≠ 0`, so the Ocneanu trace on `H₂(ℚ)` is a\ngenuinely **non-multiplicative** functional (witnessing non-vacuity of\n`ocneanuTrace_mul_defect`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeRankTwoMarkov.Hecke2.ocneanuTrace_mul_defect","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeRankTwoMarkov.Hecke2.ocneanuTrace_mul_defect","kind":"theorem","line":236,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeRankTwoMarkov.lean#L236-L246","doc":"**The multiplicativity defect equals the Hecke quadratic.**  The trace is\nmultiplicative on `σ` (`tr(σ²) = tr(σ)²`) exactly when `z` is a root of the\nHecke quadratic `X² - h·X - 1`.  Generically it is not, so the trace is a\ngenuinely non-multiplicative functional — the whole point of a Markov trace. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeRankTwoMarkov.Hecke2.markovParam_ne_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeRankTwoMarkov.Hecke2.markovParam_ne_iff","kind":"theorem","line":226,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeRankTwoMarkov.lean#L226-L234","doc":"The two Markov parameters differ **iff** the bandwidth is nonzero, i.e. iff\n`q ≠ 1`.  (The symmetric-group witness has `h = 0`, so there `z = zinv`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeRankTwoMarkov.Hecke2.ocneanuTrace_markov_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeRankTwoMarkov.Hecke2.ocneanuTrace_markov_inv","kind":"theorem","line":216,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeRankTwoMarkov.lean#L216-L222","doc":"**(T3') Markov stabilisation by the inverse generator**, with parameter\n`zinv = z - h`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeRankTwoMarkov.Hecke2.ocneanuTrace_markov","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeRankTwoMarkov.Hecke2.ocneanuTrace_markov","kind":"theorem","line":209,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeRankTwoMarkov.lean#L209-L214","doc":"**(T3) Markov stabilisation.** For any scalar element `c·1` of the bottom of\nthe tower `H₁ = R·1`, `tr((c·1) · σ) = z · tr(c·1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeRankTwoMarkov.Hecke2.ocneanuTrace_mul_comm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeRankTwoMarkov.Hecke2.ocneanuTrace_mul_comm","kind":"theorem","line":203,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeRankTwoMarkov.lean#L203-L207","doc":"**(T1) The trace property** `tr(xy) = tr(yx)` — automatic here because `H₂`\nis commutative. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeRankTwoMarkov.Hecke2.ocneanuTrace_sigmaInv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeRankTwoMarkov.Hecke2.ocneanuTrace_sigmaInv","kind":"theorem","line":197,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeRankTwoMarkov.lean#L197-L201","doc":"The trace of the inverse generator is `z - h`; this is the second Markov\nparameter `zinv` (matching `OcneanuTrace.markovParam_inv_eq_sub`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeRankTwoMarkov.Hecke2.ocneanuTrace_sigma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeRankTwoMarkov.Hecke2.ocneanuTrace_sigma","kind":"theorem","line":193,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeRankTwoMarkov.lean#L193-L195","doc":"The trace of the generator is the Markov parameter `z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeRankTwoMarkov.Hecke2.ocneanuTrace_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeRankTwoMarkov.Hecke2.ocneanuTrace_one","kind":"theorem","line":189,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeRankTwoMarkov.lean#L189-L191","doc":"**(T2) Normalisation:** the trace of `1` is `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeRankTwoMarkov.Hecke2.ocneanuTrace_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeRankTwoMarkov.Hecke2.ocneanuTrace_apply","kind":"theorem","line":186,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeRankTwoMarkov.lean#L186-L187","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeRankTwoMarkov.Hecke2.ocneanuTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeRankTwoMarkov.Hecke2.ocneanuTrace","kind":"def","line":178,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeRankTwoMarkov.lean#L178-L184","doc":"The **Ocneanu/Markov trace** on `H₂`, with Markov parameter `z`:\n`tr(a·1 + b·σ) = a + z·b`.  It is an `R`-linear functional. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeRankTwoMarkov.Hecke2.sigmaUnit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeRankTwoMarkov.Hecke2.sigmaUnit","kind":"def","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeRankTwoMarkov.lean#L169-L174","doc":"`σ` is a unit; its inverse is `σ - h·1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeRankTwoMarkov.Hecke2.sigmaInv_mul_sigma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeRankTwoMarkov.Hecke2.sigmaInv_mul_sigma","kind":"theorem","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeRankTwoMarkov.lean#L166-L167","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeRankTwoMarkov.Hecke2.sigma_mul_sigmaInv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeRankTwoMarkov.Hecke2.sigma_mul_sigmaInv","kind":"theorem","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeRankTwoMarkov.lean#L162-L164","doc":"`σ⁻¹` is a genuine two-sided inverse of `σ` (using the quadratic relation). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeRankTwoMarkov.Hecke2.sigma_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeRankTwoMarkov.Hecke2.sigma_sq","kind":"theorem","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeRankTwoMarkov.lean#L158-L160","doc":"**The Hecke quadratic relation** `σ² = h·σ + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeRankTwoMarkov.Hecke2.sigmaInv_gen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeRankTwoMarkov.Hecke2.sigmaInv_gen","kind":"theorem","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeRankTwoMarkov.lean#L156-L156","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeRankTwoMarkov.Hecke2.sigmaInv_const","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeRankTwoMarkov.Hecke2.sigmaInv_const","kind":"theorem","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeRankTwoMarkov.lean#L155-L155","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeRankTwoMarkov.Hecke2.sigma_gen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeRankTwoMarkov.Hecke2.sigma_gen","kind":"theorem","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeRankTwoMarkov.lean#L154-L154","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeRankTwoMarkov.Hecke2.sigma_const","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeRankTwoMarkov.Hecke2.sigma_const","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeRankTwoMarkov.lean#L153-L153","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeRankTwoMarkov.Hecke2.sigmaInv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeRankTwoMarkov.Hecke2.sigmaInv","kind":"def","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeRankTwoMarkov.lean#L150-L151","doc":"The inverse generator `σ⁻¹ = σ - h·1 = -h·1 + 1·σ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeRankTwoMarkov.Hecke2.sigma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeRankTwoMarkov.Hecke2.sigma","kind":"def","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeRankTwoMarkov.lean#L147-L148","doc":"The Hecke generator `σ = 0·1 + 1·σ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeRankTwoMarkov.Hecke2.instAlgebra","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeRankTwoMarkov.Hecke2.instAlgebra","kind":"instance","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeRankTwoMarkov.lean#L134-L143","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeRankTwoMarkov.Hecke2.instCommRing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeRankTwoMarkov.Hecke2.instCommRing","kind":"instance","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeRankTwoMarkov.lean#L120-L132","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeRankTwoMarkov.Hecke2.instAddGroupWithOne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeRankTwoMarkov.Hecke2.instAddGroupWithOne","kind":"instance","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeRankTwoMarkov.lean#L117-L118","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeRankTwoMarkov.Hecke2.instAddCommGroup","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeRankTwoMarkov.Hecke2.instAddCommGroup","kind":"instance","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeRankTwoMarkov.lean#L104-L115","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeRankTwoMarkov.Hecke2.smul_gen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeRankTwoMarkov.Hecke2.smul_gen","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeRankTwoMarkov.lean#L100-L100","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeRankTwoMarkov.Hecke2.smul_const","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeRankTwoMarkov.Hecke2.smul_const","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeRankTwoMarkov.lean#L99-L99","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeRankTwoMarkov.Hecke2.mul_gen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeRankTwoMarkov.Hecke2.mul_gen","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeRankTwoMarkov.lean#L97-L98","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeRankTwoMarkov.Hecke2.mul_const","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeRankTwoMarkov.Hecke2.mul_const","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeRankTwoMarkov.lean#L95-L96","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeRankTwoMarkov.Hecke2.neg_gen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeRankTwoMarkov.Hecke2.neg_gen","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeRankTwoMarkov.lean#L94-L94","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeRankTwoMarkov.Hecke2.neg_const","@type":